<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Herakleopolis Magna</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ihnasya el-Medina, Heracleopolis Magna, Nen-nesut</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Herakleopolis Magna was an ancient Egyptian city south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faiyum">Faiyum</a>, near modern Beni Suef, and capital of the 20th <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nome">nome</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-egypt">Upper Egypt</a>. Around 2160 BCE its rulers founded the Ninth and Tenth Dynasties, which ruled much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-intermediate-period">First Intermediate Period</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mentuhotep-ii">Mentuhotep II</a> of Thebes reunited the country. It was later a centre of Libyan chiefs in the Third Intermediate Period.</p></div>
